---
description: Keep agent replies clear, structured, and easy to scan
alwaysApply: true
---

# Reply style

- Lead with the verdict or answer in 1–2 sentences; do not restate the whole task.
- Use short markdown headings for distinct topics when the reply has more than one part.
- Prefer tight bullet lists for steps, options, and comparisons; avoid long walls of prose.
- Bold sparingly — only for the few words that matter.
- Keep each point short (about 1–2 sentences) unless the user asks for depth.
- Separate “what’s done” from “what’s next” when both appear.
- Do not pad with filler closings or repeated summaries.
